course: dictionary
lesson: 8499
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and sapling is one of them. Its first meaning is a young tree with a thin trunk. Its second, which you meet in stories and poems, is a young person, often a slim young man.
explain: Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. In a nature lesson, «we planted an oak sapling by the school gate» is about a tree, because you plant trees and an oak is a tree. In a story, the words around the word will show you if a person is meant.
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence. If «a young tree» fits and still makes sense, you have found it. If it does not fit, look for the other meaning, and use a dictionary to check.
fact: A sapling is a young tree with a thin trunk, grown from a seed.
fact: «Plant a sapling» means put a young tree into the ground so it can grow.
fact: Saplings grow into trees, as the text shows: «seeds grew to saplings and saplings to trees».
fact: In stories, a sapling can mean a young person, especially a slim young man, and it stands for youth and new life.
fact: Some words are spelled the same but have different meanings, so always check the clues around them.
exercise: The class will «plant a sapling» on tree-planting day. What is a sapling? | A dead branch on the ground | *A young tree with a thin trunk | A type of seed you can eat | A large tree that is very old
exercise: «Seeds grew to saplings and saplings to trees, and leaf-mould covered the stones.» What does sapling mean here? | *A young tree | A flat stone path | A fallen autumn leaf | An old wooden fence
exercise: In a story, a character is called a sapling: «He was a tall, slim sapling with a quiet smile.» What does sapling mean here? | A bag of seeds | *A young, slim person | A bird's nest | A young tree in a garden
test: Which word shows that sapling means a tree in «we planted an oak sapling by the school gate»? | *Oak | Lesson | Garden | Gate
test: «The sapling walked into the hall, tall and slim, with a quiet smile.» What does sapling mean? | A river bank | *A young, slim person | A rubbish bin | A young tree with roots in the hall
exam: Which sentence uses sapling to mean a young tree? | He was a slim sapling with a kind smile. | The sapling laughed and ran to meet her friends. | *The gardener dug a hole and planted a sapling.
